    "title": "Siouxland turns in 18K+ pounds of medications for National Drug Take Back Day - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By TIM SEAMAN Maren Ewertz ,\n1 hours ago\nIA , NE , SD ( KCAU ) — KCAU 9 regularly reports on what are known as “Drug Take Back Days,” and if you have ever wondered just how much medication is collected at those events, you may be surprised.\nIn October, on National Prescription Take Back Day, people across Iowa, Nebraska, and South Dakota turned in a total of 18,710 pounds of unneeded and expired medications.\nStory continues below\nIf you were unable to participate, but have unused prescriptions, there are nearly 16,000 pharmacies, hospitals, and businesses, as well as numerous police departments, that all offer safe medication disposal year-round.\nYou can click here to find a location near you.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to SiouxlandProud | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
